    {
      "id": "s05",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "narration": "Chapter one. Before a model sees a single word, it sees tokens.",
      "durationFrames": 150,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {"number": "01", "title": "Tokens", "subtitle": "splitting the text", "color": "blue"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "type": "DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "A tokenizer chops text into common chunks - whole words, word-pieces, sometimes single characters. Then each chunk is mapped to a number, an id the model can work with.",
      "durationFrames": 360,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "push",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Text into [tokens.]",
        "headlineColor": "purple",
        "diagram": {
          "layout": "flow",
          "nodes": [
            {"id": "raw", "label": "Raw text", "asset": "lucide:type", "color": "blue", "atWord": 1},
            {"id": "tk", "label": "Tokenizer", "asset": "lucide:scissors", "color": "purple", "atWord": 3},
            {"id": "pieces", "label": "Token pieces", "asset": "lucide:puzzle", "color": "orange", "atWord": 8},
            {"id": "ids", "label": "Token IDs", "asset": "lucide:hash", "color": "green", "atWord": 20}
          ],
          "edges": [
            {"from": "raw", "to": "tk", "atWord": 3},
            {"from": "tk", "to": "pieces", "atWord": 8},
            {"from": "pieces", "to": "ids", "atWord": 20}
          ]
        },
        "source": "TOKENIZATION: TEXT TO TOKEN IDS"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "type": "STAT_CALLOUT",
      "narration": "Every token maps to a slot in a fixed vocabulary. A typical model knows on the order of one hundred thousand distinct tokens.",
      "durationFrames": 276,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "iris",
      "data": {
        "value": 100000,
        "label": "tokens in a typical vocabulary",
        "atWord": 15,
        "source": "ILLUSTRATIVE VOCABULARY SIZE"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "narration": "Chapter two. Numbers alone mean nothing. So each token becomes a vector - a list of numbers that captures meaning.",
      "durationFrames": 168,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {"number": "02", "title": "Embeddings", "subtitle": "meaning as numbers", "color": "purple"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "type": "DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "This is embedding. The token id is looked up in a giant learned table, returning hundreds of numbers that place the word in a space of meaning.",
      "durationFrames": 330,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "push",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Meaning as [vectors.]",
        "headlineColor": "green",
        "diagram": {
          "layout": "flow",
          "nodes": [
            {"id": "id", "label": "Token ID", "asset": "lucide:hash", "color": "blue", "atWord": 4},
            {"id": "table", "label": "Lookup table", "asset": "lucide:table", "color": "purple", "atWord": 8},
            {"id": "vec", "label": "A vector", "asset": "lucide:locate", "color": "green", "atWord": 12},
            {"id": "space", "label": "Meaning-space", "asset": "lucide:box", "color": "orange", "atWord": 18}
          ],
          "edges": [
            {"from": "id", "to": "table", "atWord": 8},
            {"from": "table", "to": "vec", "atWord": 12},
            {"from": "vec", "to": "space", "atWord": 18}
          ]
        },
        "source": "EMBEDDING: TOKENS TO VECTORS"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "type": "KINETIC_TEXT",
      "narration": "In that space, similar words sit close together. Words become directions you can actually do math with.",
      "durationFrames": 246,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "fade",
      "data": {
        "kinetic": {"fx": "highlight", "text": "Words become [directions].", "sub": "similar meanings sit close", "color": "green", "atWord": 9}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "type": "CONCEPT_DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "The classic example: take the vector for king, subtract man, add woman, and you land right next to queen. The geometry encodes relationships.",
      "durationFrames": 312,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "slide",
      "data": {
        "headline": "King minus [man.]",
        "headlineColor": "purple",
        "anim": "rise",
        "nodes": [
          {"id": "king", "label": "king", "asset": "lucide:crown", "atWord": 6},
          {"id": "woman", "label": "woman", "asset": "lucide:user", "atWord": 11},
          {"id": "queen", "label": "queen", "asset": "lucide:gem", "atWord": 15}
        ],
        "edges": [
          {"from": "king", "to": "queen", "atWord": 15},
          {"from": "woman", "to": "queen", "atWord": 15}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "narration": "Chapter three. Now the key insight that made modern models possible: attention.",
      "durationFrames": 150,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {"number": "03", "title": "Attention", "subtitle": "what matters, when", "color": "orange"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "type": "DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "For each word, the model asks every other word how relevant it is. It sends a query, compares it against keys, and blends the values from the words that matter most.",
      "durationFrames": 366,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "push",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Query, key, [value.]",
        "headlineColor": "blue",
        "diagram": {
          "layout": "flow",
          "nodes": [
            {"id": "q", "label": "Query", "asset": "lucide:help-circle", "color": "blue", "atWord": 10},
            {"id": "k", "label": "Compare keys", "asset": "lucide:key", "color": "purple", "atWord": 14},
            {"id": "w", "label": "Weights", "asset": "lucide:sliders", "color": "orange", "atWord": 18},
            {"id": "v", "label": "Blend values", "asset": "lucide:layers", "color": "green", "atWord": 22}
          ],
          "edges": [
            {"from": "q", "to": "k", "label": "match", "atWord": 14, "color": "blue"},
            {"from": "k", "to": "w", "label": "score", "atWord": 18, "color": "purple"},
            {"from": "w", "to": "v", "label": "weighted", "atWord": 22, "color": "orange"}
          ]
        },
        "source": "SELF-ATTENTION: QUERY, KEY, VALUE"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "type": "DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "Do that for every word at once, and each token gathers context from the entire sentence - not just its immediate neighbors.",
      "durationFrames": 300,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "iris",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Attend to [all.]",
        "headlineColor": "orange",
        "diagram": {
          "layout": "hub",
          "nodes": [
            {"id": "cur", "label": "This token", "asset": "lucide:crosshair", "color": "orange", "atWord": 8},
            {"id": "w1", "label": "The", "asset": "lucide:type", "color": "blue", "atWord": 12},
            {"id": "w2", "label": "cat", "asset": "lucide:type", "color": "purple", "atWord": 12},
            {"id": "w3", "label": "sat", "asset": "lucide:type", "color": "green", "atWord": 13},
            {"id": "w4", "label": "quietly", "asset": "lucide:type", "color": "yellow", "atWord": 13}
          ]
        },
        "source": "EACH TOKEN ATTENDS TO ALL OTHERS"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "type": "QUOTE_SPOTLIGHT",
      "narration": "The 2017 paper that introduced this architecture said it best, right in its title.",
      "durationFrames": 258,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "dip",
      "fx": "vignette",
      "data": {
        "person": {"name": "Vaswani et al., 2017", "role": "The Transformer paper"},
        "quote": "Attention is all you need.",
        "source": "THE PAPER THAT INTRODUCED THE TRANSFORMER"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "narration": "Chapter four. Attention is the engine. The transformer is the machine built around it.",
      "durationFrames": 156,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {"number": "04", "title": "The Transformer", "subtitle": "the stack", "color": "blue"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "type": "DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "One block does two things in turn: an attention layer to mix information across words, then a feed-forward layer to think about each word on its own. Stack dozens of these, and you get a deep model.",
      "durationFrames": 372,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "push",
      "data": {
        "headline": "One block, [stacked.]",
        "headlineColor": "purple",
        "diagram": {
          "layout": "block",
          "nodes": [
            {"id": "att", "label": "Attention", "asset": "lucide:eye", "color": "blue", "atWord": 10, "col": 0, "row": 0},
            {"id": "n1", "label": "Add + norm", "asset": "lucide:plus", "color": "green", "atWord": 12, "col": 0, "row": 1},
            {"id": "ff", "label": "Feed-forward", "asset": "lucide:cpu", "color": "orange", "atWord": 16, "col": 0, "row": 2},
            {"id": "n2", "label": "Add + norm", "asset": "lucide:plus", "color": "green", "atWord": 20, "col": 0, "row": 3}
          ],
          "edges": [
            {"from": "att", "to": "n1", "atWord": 12},
            {"from": "n1", "to": "ff", "atWord": 16},
            {"from": "ff", "to": "n2", "atWord": 20}
          ]
        },
        "source": "A TRANSFORMER BLOCK, STACKED N TIMES"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "type": "STAT_PANELS",
      "narration": "Scale is the other half of the story. Modern models stack many layers and carry billions of parameters - the adjustable weights that store everything they've learned.",
      "durationFrames": 336,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "fade",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Built at [scale.]",
        "headlineColor": "orange",
        "stats": [
          {"kicker": "DEPTH", "value": "dozens", "color": "blue", "atWord": 9},
          {"kicker": "PARAMETERS", "value": "billions", "color": "purple", "atWord": 13}
        ],
        "verdict": {"text": "weights are the memory", "color": "orange", "atWord": 18},
        "source": "ILLUSTRATIVE MODEL SCALE"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "type": "PHOTO",
      "narration": "And none of this is abstract. It all runs on real hardware - warehouses of GPUs, humming day and night to train and serve these models.",
      "durationFrames": 288,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "fx": "letterbox",
      "data": {
        "photo": {"asset": "img:server-racks.jpg", "kicker": "THE COMPUTE", "caption": "Warehouses of GPUs, running nonstop", "color": "blue", "pan": "in", "atWord": 1},
        "source": "PHOTO: WIKIMEDIA / VIRTUO DOC - CC BY-SA 4.0"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "narration": "Chapter five. A fresh model knows nothing at all. Training is how it learns - by reading.",
      "durationFrames": 156,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {"number": "05", "title": "Training", "subtitle": "learning from text", "color": "green"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "type": "DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "Training is a loop. Show the model text with the next word hidden, let it guess, measure how wrong it was, and nudge every weight to be a little less wrong. Then repeat.",
      "durationFrames": 384,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "push",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Guess, check, [adjust.]",
        "headlineColor": "green",
        "diagram": {
          "layout": "flow",
          "nodes": [
            {"id": "hide", "label": "Hide next word", "asset": "lucide:eye-off", "color": "blue", "atWord": 6},
            {"id": "guess", "label": "Model guesses", "asset": "lucide:brain-circuit", "color": "purple", "atWord": 12},
            {"id": "err", "label": "Measure error", "asset": "lucide:ruler", "color": "orange", "atWord": 16},
            {"id": "adj", "label": "Adjust weights", "asset": "lucide:sliders", "color": "green", "atWord": 22}
          ],
          "edges": [
            {"from": "hide", "to": "guess", "atWord": 12},
            {"from": "guess", "to": "err", "atWord": 16},
            {"from": "err", "to": "adj", "atWord": 22}
          ]
        },
        "source": "GRADIENT DESCENT: THE TRAINING LOOP"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "type": "KINETIC_TEXT",
      "narration": "Wrong. Adjust. Wrong again. Adjust again. Across trillions of words, the errors shrink and fluent language emerges.",
      "durationFrames": 252,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "fade",
      "data": {
        "kinetic": {"fx": "glitch", "text": "Wrong. Adjust. Repeat.", "sub": "a trillion times over", "color": "red", "atWord": 1}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "type": "BAR_COMPARE",
      "narration": "There are two phases. Pretraining reads a vast slice of the internet to learn language itself. Fine-tuning then shapes behavior with a much smaller, carefully curated set.",
      "durationFrames": 354,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "iris",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Two [phases.]",
        "headlineColor": "blue",
        "bars": [
          {"label": "Pretraining", "value": 100, "display": "massive", "color": "blue", "atWord": 6},
          {"label": "Fine-tuning", "value": 12, "display": "curated", "color": "green", "atWord": 16}
        ],
        "maxValue": 100,
        "source": "ILLUSTRATIVE RELATIVE DATA SCALE"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "type": "CHAT_MOCKUP",
      "narration": "One fine-tuning step uses people directly. Humans compare answers and rank them, teaching the model which kinds of responses we actually prefer.",
      "durationFrames": 324,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "fade",
      "data": {
        "messages": [
          {"from": "agent", "text": "Here are two answers. Which is better?", "atWord": 1},
          {"from": "user", "text": "The second one - it's clearer.", "color": "green", "atWord": 9},
          {"from": "agent", "text": "Understood. I'll favor that style.", "color": "blue", "atWord": 14}
        ],
        "source": "RLHF: LEARNING FROM HUMAN PREFERENCES"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s24b",
      "type": "SUBSCRIBE_REMINDER",
      "narration": "If the pieces are clicking into place, subscribe - we go this deep every single week.",
      "durationFrames": 210,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "wipe",
      "fx": "burst",
      "data": {
        "subscribe": {"text": "Making sense so far?", "sub": "we go this deep every week", "handle": "@yourchannel", "color": "orange", "atWord": 1}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "type": "CHAPTER",
      "narration": "Chapter six. Now the payoff: how a trained model actually writes.",
      "durationFrames": 150,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "dip",
      "data": {
        "chapter": {"number": "06", "title": "Generation", "subtitle": "writing back", "color": "orange"}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "type": "DIAGRAM",
      "narration": "Generation happens one token at a time. The model reads everything so far, predicts the next token, appends it, and feeds the whole thing back in to predict the one after that.",
      "durationFrames": 372,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "push",
      "data": {
        "headline": "One token at a [time.]",
        "headlineColor": "blue",
        "diagram": {
          "layout": "flow",
          "nodes": [
            {"id": "prompt", "label": "Prompt so far", "asset": "lucide:message-square", "color": "blue", "atWord": 6},
            {"id": "pred", "label": "Predict token", "asset": "lucide:brain-circuit", "color": "orange", "atWord": 12},
            {"id": "app", "label": "Append it", "asset": "lucide:plus", "color": "green", "atWord": 16},
            {"id": "loop", "label": "Feed back", "asset": "lucide:repeat", "color": "purple", "atWord": 22}
          ],
          "edges": [
            {"from": "prompt", "to": "pred", "atWord": 12},
            {"from": "pred", "to": "app", "atWord": 16},
            {"from": "app", "to": "loop", "atWord": 22}
          ]
        },
        "source": "AUTOREGRESSIVE GENERATION"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s27",
      "type": "SOUND_WAVE",
      "narration": "That's why answers stream in, word by word. Each pulse you see appear is one more token, chosen and printed.",
      "durationFrames": 288,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "transition": "fade",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Word by [word.]",
        "headlineColor": "blue",
        "wave": {"label": "streaming tokens", "color": "blue", "atWord": 1},
        "source": "TOKENS ARE STREAMED AS THEY ARE PICKED"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s28",
      "type": "SPLIT_PATHS",
      "narration": "But which token? Always taking the single most likely gives safe, repetitive text. Sampling with a little randomness - tuned by a dial called temperature - gives creativity and surprise.",
      "durationFrames": 366,
      "timingSource": "estimated",
      "background": "zoneB",
      "transition": "slide",
      "data": {
        "headline": "Safe vs [creative.]",
        "headlineColor": "purple",
        "center": {"kicker": "NEXT TOKEN", "title": "many options", "color": "blue", "atWord": 4},
        "left": {
          "title": "Greedy",
          "badge": {"text": "TEMP 0", "color": "blue"},
          "lines": [{"text": "always the top pick", "color": "blue"}, {"text": "safe, repetitive", "color": "green"}],
          "color": "blue",
          "atWord": 1
        },
        "right": {
          "title": "Sampling",
          "badge": {"text": "TEMP > 0", "color": "orange"},
          "lines": [{"text": "weighted random pick", "color": "orange"}, {"text": "creative, varied", "color": "green"}],
          "color": "orange",
          "atWord": 12
        },
        "source": "DECODING: GREEDY VS TEMPERATURE SAMPLING"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s29",
